    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="22.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAtr">VI Atr</ref> 22.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="22.2" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="252" ed="#liebermann"/>K. ⁊ s<hi rend="italic">anct</hi>a Marian heahfreolstida ealle weorðige man georne, ærest mid fæstene ⁊ syþþan mid freolse.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="22.2" corresp="#wit-d-incomplete"><pb n="252" ed="#liebermann"/>And s<hi rend="italic">anct</hi>a Marian freolstida wurðige man georne, ærost mid fæstene ⁊ siððan mid freolse.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="22.2" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="96" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ sancta Marian heahfreolstida<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#VIAtr_22-2.robnote.fn.7"/> ealle<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#VIAtr_22-2.robnote.fn.3"/> weorðige man georne, ærest mid fæstene ⁊ syþþan mid freolse.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="168" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And sancta Marian heahfreolstida ealle weorðige man georne, ærest mid fæstene and syþþan mid freolse.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="253" ed="#liebermann"/>Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#VIAtr_22-2.lnote.de.1"/> alle hohen Festzeiten der heiligen Maria ehre man willig, zuerst durch Fasten und dann durch Festfeier.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let all the high festivals of St Mary be eagerly honoured, first with fasting and then with feasting.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#VIAtr_22-2.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="97" ed="#robertson"/>And all St Mary's high-festivals shall be zealously honoured, first with fasting and afterwards with festivity.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="169" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And each of the Feasts of Saint Mary is to be celebrated faithfully, first with fasting and then with a holiday.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="253"><ref target="clause:VAtr_14">V Atr 14</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 14</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:ICn_16a">I Cn 16a</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#kennedy" n="59"><label>source in V–VIII Æthelred</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-040">Cn 1018 14.2–14.3</ref> <quote>Kennedy’s table: VI Æthelred 22.2, VI Æthelred 22.3 | D 14.2–14.3 | I Cnut 16a</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:ICn_16a">I Cn 16a</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 16a: Cn 1018 14:2-3  VI Atr 22:2-3, 24</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VIAtr_22-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">176</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">butan hwa wille</hi> scheint erst K einzuführen, der Askese freundlich</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">butan hwa wille</hi> seems to be introduced only by K, who is well disposed towards asceticism</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">On several rubrics: VI Atr 22, 2; 3</note></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VIAtr_22-2.lnote.de.0" n="0" source="#liebermann-erkl" rend="wholeClause"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">176</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">benutzt durch I Cn 16—16, 1 und (?) <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 167.—</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">used by I Cn 16—16, 1 and (?) <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 167.—</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VIAtr_22-2.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">333</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">With this clause and the next cf. V, 14 f.; I Cn. 16 f.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="VIAtr_22-2.robnote.fn.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">96</biblScope></bibl><label>⁊</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Om. D.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="VIAtr_22-2.robnote.fn.7" n="7" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">96</biblScope></bibl><label>heahfreolstida</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">freolst.</hi> D.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
